# ldconfig — real-world examples

## Reload the shared library cache (/etc/ld.so.cache)

```sh
sudo ldconfig
```

## Print every library currently in the cache

```sh
ldconfig -p
ldconfig -p | grep libssl     # is a specific lib registered, and where?
```

## Homelab: make a library in /usr/local/lib visible

```sh
# After installing something from source onto homelab:
echo '/usr/local/lib' | sudo tee /etc/ld.so.conf.d/local.conf
sudo ldconfig
```

## Homelab: debug "error while loading shared libraries"

```sh
ldd /usr/local/bin/mytool      # which libs does it want, which are missing?
ldconfig -p | grep libfoo      # is the missing lib in the cache at all?
```

## Verbose run — show directories scanned and links made

```sh
sudo ldconfig -v | less
```

| Flag | What it does                              |
| ---- | ----------------------------------------- |
| (none) | rebuild /etc/ld.so.cache                |
| -p   | print the current cache                   |
| -v   | verbose — list dirs and libraries found   |
| -n <dir> | process only the given directory      |
